  "ActionRequest scoped FKs take implicit FOR KEY SHARE on the referenced Connection/ApiToken rows at insert; an owner key-changing delete/move racing an admission can deadlock -> ACTION_DB_CONFLICT (no retry). Explicit row locks are not taken.",
  "Per-admission readiness SQL scans catalog privileges (tens of ms in tests); acceptable for CLI scale, review for API scale.",
  "Implementation choices for review: ACTION_NOT_FOUND (unknown/invisible request ID, not in the 02 list) and ACTION_STATE_CONFLICT for derived-ID collisions; validity hints CURRENT/NOT_PENDING/AUTHORITY_CHANGED/SIGNER_EXPIRED; version strings atlas-action-policy/1 and atlas-synthetic-ticket-port/1; idempotency key must be a lower-case UUID.",
  "Later-stage tables (approval/attempt/verification/mock) carry the 04 state machine as DB lifecycle triggers now; S3-B/C semantics that differ need a reviewed migration. DB caps approval expiry by the approver snapshot only; the requester-snapshot cap is an S3-B service duty.",
  "Owner DDL bypass (disabling triggers, replacing function bodies as superuser) is outside supported operation; readiness detects disabled/origin-only triggers, ACL/owner/policy/grant drift, not function-body replacement.",
  "Expiry comparisons use clock_timestamp() AT TIME ZONE UTC (codebase convention: timestamp columns hold UTC).",
  "A seed re-run without tokens performs no writes (Prisma upsert with empty update), so it does not move the epoch; with a token it does.",
  "scripts/pg17-check.ts not extended with action invariants; the PG17 action surface is covered by test:pg."
 ],
